{
  "title": "Travel and transport",
  "note": "Use en with vehicles (en tren, en autobús, en avión) but a pie for on foot. Salir (to leave) has an irregular yo form: salgo; the rest are regular: sales, sale, salimos, salen. Some words vary: el coche (Spain) is usually el carro or el auto in Latin America, and el billete (ticket) is often el boleto there.",
  "src": {"t": "Spanish 1A: Beginning Spanish (LibreTexts)", "u": "https://human.libretexts.org/Courses/Chabot_College/Spanish_1A%3A_Beginning_Spanish_(2026)"},
